Launch the configured shell on Windows

QTermWidget::setShellProgram() is documented public API and, on Windows, did
nothing at all. Session::run()'s Windows branch opened by assigning over
whatever the caller had configured:

    QString exec = QStringLiteral("C:\WINDOWS\System32\WindowsPowerShell\v1.0\powershell.exe");
    if(!QFile(exec).exists())
        exec = QStringLiteral("C:\WINDOWS\system32\cmd.exe");

_program is never read, so every terminal got PowerShell no matter what was
asked for. The Unix branch immediately above does the opposite -- it starts from
_program and falls back only when that is empty or missing -- so this restores
the same shape: honour _program, resolve a bare name through PATH because
ConPtyProcess requires an absolute path, and fall back to PowerShell, then
%ComSpec%, then cmd.exe. Consulting ComSpec before hardcoding cmd.exe is a small
addition; the previous code assumed C:\WINDOWS.

The second half is why fixing the first half alone still does not work.
Session::run() builds `arguments` starting with the program itself, following
the argv[0] convention the Unix path wants. ConPtyProcess::startProcess() then
prepends the shell path to whatever list it is given, so the program is named
twice and the second copy arrives as an argument. With PowerShell that is
harmless enough to go unnoticed; point it at a shell and the shell is asked to
execute itself as a script:

    C:/dev/msys64/usr/bin/bash.exe: C:/dev/msys64/usr/bin/bash.exe:
        cannot execute binary file

Hence arguments.mid(1).

This is NOT the cause of the unanswered report on the PR that
startTerminalTeletype "is not work", though it looks like a candidate at first:

    https://github.com/lxqt/qtermwidget/pull/578#issuecomment-3009278241

That path never reaches this code. Session::runEmptyPTY() does not call
Pty::start() at all -- it calls Pty::setEmptyPTYProperties(), which the Windows
branch leaves as an empty stub. ConPTY has no pty-without-a-process to hand a
caller, so there is nothing obvious for it to do, and making that mode work
needs a design decision rather than a fix. Left alone here.

Not fixed here, and worth knowing about: ConPtyProcess::startProcess() builds
its command line by joining the path and arguments with spaces and no quoting,
so a shell whose path contains a space -- anything under C:\Program Files --
will still be split. Correct Windows command-line quoting is a bigger change
than this patch wants to be.

Verified live together with 0007: an MSYS2 bash comes up with its own prompt,
the correct working directory, colours and bracketed paste.

Upstream: not submitted; belongs on PR #578, which is not being merged --
         see 0001's header
Applies-to: all environments (the changed code is behind Q_OS_WIN)

